summary:
  The homepage reader looks into a tag of any length.

history:
  A homepage comes from a record anyone can file and the popup reads it with
  no click. The old patterns ran over a head of "<meta/name='og:image'" with
  no ">" for 139 s on Qt 6.12 and the shell froze with them; the reader now
  takes one tag at a time, never past the next "<" and never longer than
  MAX_TAG.

target:
  package/contents/ui/FaviconLogic.js

find:
      const tagRe = new RegExp("<(link|meta)\\b([^<>]{0," + MAX_TAG + "})>", "gi");

replace:
      const tagRe = new RegExp("<(link|meta)\\b([^<>]*)>", "gi");

expect:
  Killed by tst_faviconlogic::test_a_tag_past_the_cap_is_passed_over_and_the_next_one_read.
  Line-neutral.
